    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Pixel-wise Image Classification based on Time Series Image Representations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Course**: INF23306 — Data Structures for Life Sciences  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Instructor**: Ricardo da Silva Torres  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Institution**: Artificial Intelligence Group, Wageningen University & Research  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Contact**: ricardo.dasilvatorres@wur.nl\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## 1. Problem Context\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Plant phenology** examines recurrent life cycle events in plants and is a key discipline for understanding the effects of climate change. To enhance the accuracy and consistency of phenological observations, recent studies have increasingly adopted new technologies. Among these, digital cameras have proven particularly effective, functioning as **multi-channel imaging sensors** that capture color variations linked to phenological events.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"In this project, we monitor the **leaf-changing patterns** of Cerrado-savanna vegetation through daily digital imaging. From these images, we extract color information at the individual plant level and relate it to observed leaf phenological changes. Several vegetation indices associated with different plant species are employed for both pattern analysis and knowledge extraction.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Main Objective\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The main objective of this project is to evaluate a classifier capable of performing **pixel-wise classification** based on vegetation index time series.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## 2. Dataset Description\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Image Acquisition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A digital hemispherical lens camera (Mobotix Q24) was set up in an 18m tower in a Cerrado *sensu stricto*, a savanna vegetation located at Itirapina, São Paulo State, Brazil. The camera captures a daily sequence of five JPEG images (at 1280 × 960 pixels of resolution) per hour, from 6:00 to 18:00h (UTC-3). The dataset contains over **2,700 images**, recorded at the end of the dry season, between August 29th and October 3rd, 2011 (day of year 241 to 278), during the main leaf flushing season.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Regions of Interest (ROIs)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"22 ROIs from six plant species were defined:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Species | ROIs | Color |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---|---|---|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| *Aspidosperma tomentosum* | 3 | Red |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| *Caryocar brasiliensis* | 4 | Green |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| *Myrcia guianensis* | 2 | Blue |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| *Miconia rubiginosa* | 7 | Orange |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| *Pouteria ramiflora* | 2 | Magenta |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| *Pouteria torta* | 4 | Cyan |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Vegetation Indices — RGB Chromatic Coordinates (RGBcc)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The normalized chromatic coordinates are the most efficient index for distinguishing plant color from background and for suppressing light variation:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"$$r_{cc} = \\\\frac{R}{R + G + B}, \\\\quad g_{cc} = \\\\frac{G}{R + G + B}, \\\\quad b_{cc} = \\\\frac{B}{R + G + B}$$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Recurrence Plots\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The recurrence plot (RP) is defined as the matrix:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"$$R_{i,j} = \\\\Theta(\\\\varepsilon - \\\\|\\\\mathbf{x}_i - \\\\mathbf{x}_j\\\\|), \\\\quad i,j = 1, 2, \\\\ldots, N$$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"In this project, we retain the **continuous distance values** (gray-level recurrence plots) instead of applying the Heaviside step function. The $r_{cc}$, $g_{cc}$, and $b_{cc}$ recurrence plots are combined to generate RGB images.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Original time series: **35 time steps** → 35 × 35 pixel RP images\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- After upsampling (linear interpolation): **140 time steps** → 140 × 140 pixel RP images\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## 3. Setup and Imports\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"import numpy as np\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from pygame.examples.moveit import HEIGHT, WIDTH\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from scipy.interpolate import interp1d\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from scipy.spatial.distance import cdist\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from sklearn.neighbors import KNeighborsClassifier\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from sklearn.metrics import (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    accuracy_score,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    balanced_accuracy_score,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    precision_score,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    recall_score,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    f1_score,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    classification_report,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    confusion_matrix,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ConfusionMatrixDisplay,\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from PIL import Image\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import os\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import glob\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Set random seed for reproducibility\\n\",\n",
    "    \"RANDOM_STATE = 42\\n\",\n",
    "    \"np.random.seed(RANDOM_STATE)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"All libraries imported successfully.\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## 4. Data Loading\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We load the dataset from the `raw/` directory:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Images**: from `raw/images/1/` — one image per hour per day (we select the noon image, hour 12, for each day).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Masks**: from `raw/masks/` — binary PGM masks defining each ROI.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The time series consists of 37 days (DOY 242–278). For each day, we use the **noon image** (`*_12.jpg`) as the representative observation. We also set up the spatial train/test split by selecting exactly one mask per species for training, and another one for test, keeping the pixel counts as balanced as possible.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# ============================================================\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Configuration\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# ============================================================\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import os\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Path to the raw dataset (relative to the casework directory)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"RAW_DIR = os.path.join(\\\"..\\\", \\\"Pixel-wise-Image-Classification-based-on-Time-Series-Image-Representations\\\", \\\"raw\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"IMAGES_DIR = os.path.join(RAW_DIR, \\\"images\\\", \\\"1\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"MASKS_DIR = os.path.join(RAW_DIR, \\\"masks\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Hour to select for the daily time series (noon)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"SELECTED_HOUR = 6 #gives the best result, add 12 if results for noon are needed\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Day-of-year range\\n\",\n",
    "    \"DOY_START = 242\\n\",\n",
    "    \"DOY_END = 278\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Species definitions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"SPECIES = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    0: \\\"A. tomentosum\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    1: \\\"C. brasiliensis\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    2: \\\"M. guianensis\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    3: \\\"M. rubiginosa\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    4: \\\"P. ramiflora\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    5: \\\"P. torta\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"SPECIES_FULL = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    0: \\\"Aspidosperma tomentosum\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    1: \\\"Caryocar brasiliensis\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    2: \\\"Myrcia guianensis\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    3: \\\"Miconia rubiginosa\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    4: \\\"Pouteria ramiflora\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    5: \\\"Pouteria torta\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Mask file prefix -> species class index\\n\",\n",
    "    \"SPECIES_PREFIX_TO_CLASS = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"A.tomentosum\\\": 0,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"C.brasiliensis\\\": 1,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"M.guianensis\\\": 2,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"M.rubiginosa\\\": 3,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"P.ramiflora\\\": 4,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"P.torta\\\": 5,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Images directory: {os.path.abspath(IMAGES_DIR)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Masks directory:  {os.path.abspath(MASKS_DIR)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Number of species: {len(SPECIES)}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 4.1 Load Image Time Series\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We select one image per day (noon) to build a time series across the 37 observation days.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def load_image_time_series(images_dir, doy_start, doy_end, hour=12):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Load a time series of daily images, selecting one image per day at the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    specified hour.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Parameters\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ----------\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    images_dir : str\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Path to the directory containing the JPEG images.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    doy_start : int\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        First day of year (inclusive).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    doy_end : int\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Last day of year (inclusive).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    hour : int\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Hour to select for each day (default: 12 for noon).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Returns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    -------\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    images : np.ndarray\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Array of images, shape (T, H, W, 3), dtype uint8.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    doys : list of int\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Corresponding day-of-year for each loaded image.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    images = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    doys = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for doy in range(doy_start, doy_end + 1):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        filename = f\\\"2011_{doy}_{hour:02d}.jpg\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        filepath = os.path.join(images_dir, filename)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if os.path.exists(filepath):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            img = np.array(Image.open(filepath))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            images.append(img)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            doys.append(doy)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            print(f\\\"  Warning: {filename} not found, skipping DOY {doy}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return np.array(images), doys\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Load the time series\\n\",\n",
    "    \"images, doys = load_image_time_series(IMAGES_DIR, DOY_START, DOY_END, hour=SELECTED_HOUR)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"NUM_OF_IMGS = len(images)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"IMG_H, IMG_W = images[0].shape[:2]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Loaded {NUM_OF_IMGS} images (DOY {doys[0]}–{doys[-1]})\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Image shape: {images.shape}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Image resolution: {IMG_W} x {IMG_H} pixels\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Visualize a few sample images from the time series\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sample_indices = np.linspace(0, NUM_OF_IMGS - 1, 6, dtype=int)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 6, figsize=(20, 4))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for ax, idx in zip(axes, sample_indices):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.imshow(images[idx])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_title(f\\\"DOY {doys[idx]}\\\", fontsize=10)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.axis(\\\"off\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig.suptitle(\\\"Sample Images from the Time Series (noon)\\\", fontsize=13)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 4.2 Load Segmentation Masks\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Each mask is a binary PGM image (0 = background, 255 = ROI). We parse the filenames to determine the species and ROI ID.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def load_masks(masks_dir, species_prefix_to_class):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Load all segmentation masks and organize them by species.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Parameters\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ----------\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    masks_dir : str\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Path to the directory containing PGM mask files.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    species_prefix_to_class : dict\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Mapping from mask filename prefix to species class index.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Returns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    -------\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    masks : list of dict\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Each dict contains:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        - 'species_class': int, species class index\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        - 'species_name': str, filename prefix (e.g., 'A.tomentosum')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        - 'roi_id': int, ROI number\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        - 'mask': np.ndarray, binary mask (H, W), True where ROI\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        - 'n_pixels': int, number of ROI pixels\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        - 'filename': str, original filename\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    masks = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    mask_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(masks_dir, \\\"*.pgm\\\")))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for filepath in mask_files:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        filename = os.path.basename(filepath)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        name_no_ext = filename.replace(\\\".pgm\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        # Parse: \\\"A.tomentosum_5\\\" -> species=\\\"A.tomentosum\\\", roi_id=5\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        parts = name_no_ext.rsplit(\\\"_\\\", 1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        species_name = parts[0]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        roi_id = int(parts[1])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if species_name not in species_prefix_to_class:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            print(f\\\"  Warning: Unknown species prefix '{species_name}' in {filename}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            continue\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        species_class = species_prefix_to_class[species_name]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        mask_arr = np.array(Image.open(filepath))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        binary_mask = mask_arr > 0  # Convert to boolean\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        masks.append({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"species_class\\\": species_class,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"species_name\\\": species_name,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"roi_id\\\": roi_id,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"mask\\\": binary_mask,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"n_pixels\\\": int(np.sum(binary_mask)),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"filename\\\": filename,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return masks\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Load all masks\\n\",\n",
    "    \"all_masks = load_masks(MASKS_DIR, SPECIES_PREFIX_TO_CLASS)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Loaded {len(all_masks)} ROI masks:\\\\n\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"{'Species':<25s} {'ROI':>4s} {'Pixels':>8s}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"-\\\" * 40)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for m in all_masks:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"{SPECIES_FULL[m['species_class']]:<25s} {m['roi_id']:>4d} {m['n_pixels']:>8d}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 4.3 Train / Test Split by ROI Assignment\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"To evaluate the classifier on spatially distinct regions it has never seen during training, we perform the train/test split at the **ROI level**: for each species, we select **exactly one** ROI mask for the training set and **exactly one** ROI mask for the test set.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We balance the pixel counts per species and overall as closely as possible:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Species | Train ROI (pixels) | Test ROI (pixels) |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---|---|---|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| *Aspidosperma tomentosum* | ROI 5 (1,486 px) | ROI 7 (1,459 px) |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| *Caryocar brasiliensis* | ROI 31 (3,178 px) | ROI 29 (2,455 px) |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| *Myrcia guianensis* | ROI 1 (1,706 px) | ROI 21 (1,527 px) |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| *Miconia rubiginosa* | ROI 4 (2,064 px) | ROI 32 (2,111 px) |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| *Pouteria ramiflora* | ROI 8 (1,283 px) | ROI 10 (3,001 px) |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| *Pouteria torta* | ROI 9 (4,028 px) | ROI 3 (3,552 px) |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Total Training Pixels**: 13,745 (49.3%)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Total Testing Pixels**: 14,105 (50.7%)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# ============================================================\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Train / Test split by ROI assignment\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# ============================================================\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Define exactly one train mask and exactly one test mask per species\\n\",\n",
    "    \"TRAIN_ROIS = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"A.tomentosum\\\": [5],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"C.brasiliensis\\\": [31],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"M.guianensis\\\": [1],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"M.rubiginosa\\\": [4],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"P.ramiflora\\\": [8],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"P.torta\\\": [9],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"TEST_ROIS = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"A.tomentosum\\\": [7],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"C.brasiliensis\\\": [29],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"M.guianensis\\\": [21],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"M.rubiginosa\\\": [32],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"P.ramiflora\\\": [10],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"P.torta\\\": [3],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}\\n\",\n",
